From cbcc1975876e99e98d61606977833f1c7e8a910e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lgosling <luizandre.gosling@windriver.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 11:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Escape $ in shellfilter to block command injection

The shellfilter template filter used to sanitize user-provided
values embedded in double-quoted strings inside the generated
OpenStack RC files (openrc.sh.template, ec2rc/application
credential templates) escapes backslash, backtick and quote
characters, but does not escape the dollar sign.

Since the values are interpolated inside double-quoted shell
strings, an unescaped $(...) sequence is still expanded by the
shell as a command substitution even though backticks are
escaped. A domain manager able to set a project name (or user/
domain name) containing a $() sequence can therefore have
arbitrary commands executed on the machine of any user who
sources the downloaded RC file.

Add '$' to the replacements map so it is escaped to '\$', which
neutralizes command substitution while leaving the literal
character intact when the string is echoed back.

Signed-off-by: lgosling <luizandre.gosling@windriver.com>
---
 horizon/templatetags/shellfilter.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/horizon/templatetags/shellfilter.py b/horizon/templatetags/shellfilter.py
index 167a222..44dc166 100644
--- a/horizon/templatetags/shellfilter.py
+++ b/horizon/templatetags/shellfilter.py
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ register = template.Library()
 def shellfilter(value):
     """Replace HTML chars for shell usage."""
     replacements = {'\\': '\\\\',
+                    '$': '\\$',
                     '`': '\\`',
                     "'": "\\'",
                     '"': '\\"'}
